note: The window module: open a window, draw in it, read the keys and the mouse.
note: A program uses it with the line  import window  at the top.
note:
note: This file says what the module offers. The Python code that does the work is in window_impl.py.
note:
note:   let win be Window(title: "My game", width: 640, height: 480)
note:   while open of win do
note:       run clear of win
note:       run draw_circle(320, 240, 30, orange) of win
note:       run show of win
note:   end

note: A color you make yourself:  let sky be Color(red: 20, green: 24, blue: 40)
define Color as
    red as number
    green as number
    blue as number
end

note: The color names. Red, green and blue go from 0 to 255.
let red be Color(red: 230, green: 50, blue: 50) fixed
let green be Color(red: 50, green: 180, blue: 70) fixed
let blue be Color(red: 50, green: 100, blue: 230) fixed
let yellow be Color(red: 250, green: 220, blue: 50) fixed
let orange be Color(red: 255, green: 150, blue: 30) fixed
let purple be Color(red: 150, green: 70, blue: 200) fixed
let pink be Color(red: 255, green: 130, blue: 180) fixed
let brown be Color(red: 140, green: 90, blue: 50) fixed
let gray be Color(red: 128, green: 128, blue: 128) fixed
let white be Color(red: 255, green: 255, blue: 255) fixed
let black be Color(red: 0, green: 0, blue: 0) fixed

note: The window. Making one opens it. The fields marked readonly are kept up to date by Python.
define Window as
    title as text
    width as number
    height as number
    background as Color = black
    color as Color = white
    open as boolean readonly
    mouse_x as number readonly
    mouse_y as number readonly
    mouse_down as boolean readonly
end

note: Python builds the type Window. In this file the thing is called "window".
export Window as window to python "window_impl"

note: Python provides these actions. Each one works on a window:  run clear of win
from python "window_impl"
    action close of window
    action show of window
    action clear of window
    action draw_rectangle(x as number, y as number, width as number, height as number, color as Color = color of window) of window
    action draw_circle(x as number, y as number, radius as number, color as Color = color of window) of window
    action draw_line(x1 as number, y1 as number, x2 as number, y2 as number, color as Color = color of window) of window
    action draw_text(text as text, x as number, y as number, color as Color = color of window) of window
    question is_down(key as text) of window gives boolean
end
